  <img decoding="async" width="696" height="392" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1102659188-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="Survey Finds Gen Z More Likely to Invest in Cryptocurrencies and Memes Over Traditional Investments" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1102659188-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1102659188-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1102659188-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1102659188-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1102659188-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1102659188-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1102659188-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1102659188-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1102659188-760x428.jpg 760w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/shutterstock_1102659188.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 696px) 100vw, 696px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>A recent study published by Gambler’s Pick notes that Gen Zers are less likely to invest in traditional investments like equities and more likely to invest in cryptocurrencies, meme investments, and non-fungible tokens (NFTs). </strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Gen Z More Likely to Invest in Cryptocurrencies and Meme Investments Than Stocks and Common Assets
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    <span style="font-weight: 400;">The web portal gamblerspick.com published a study at the end of April that highlights the investment choices of Gen Zers. Generation Z or Gen Z for short is a demographic that succeeds Millennials. </span>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <span style="font-weight: 400;">The group colloquially known as “zoomers,” were born between the mid-to-late 1990s and up until the early 2010s. The Gambler’s Pick survey notes that Gen Zers are more apt to invest in cryptocurrencies and NFTs over traditional stocks.</span>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-463775 size-full" title="Survey Finds Gen Z More Likely to Invest in Cryptocurrencies and Memes Over Traditional Investments " src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hiodoodhh.jpg" alt="Survey Finds Gen Z More Likely to Invest in Cryptocurrencies and Memes Over Traditional Investments " width="1280" height="900" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hiodoodhh.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hiodoodhh-300x211.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hiodoodhh-1024x720.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hiodoodhh-768x540.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hiodoodhh-100x70.jpg 100w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hiodoodhh-200x140.jpg 200w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hiodoodhh-696x489.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hiodoodhh-1068x751.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/hiodoodhh-597x420.jpg 597w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <span style="font-weight: 400;">The survey polled 872 people and 24% of the group represented Gen Z and 27% were Millennials. “25% were Gen Xers, and 24% were baby boomers or older,” the Gambler’s Pick study adds. Some key findings noted that Gen Z likes collectives but is still more likely to invest in stuff like sneakers and clothes. </span>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <span style="font-weight: 400;">Interestingly, the Gen Z crowd noted why they were investing and they mentioned fighting back “against institutions” and to “participate in a movement.”</span>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="aligncenter wp-image-463779 size-full" title="Survey Finds Gen Z More Likely to Invest in Cryptocurrencies and Memes Over Traditional Investments " src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/cryptoww3221.jpg" alt="Survey Finds Gen Z More Likely to Invest in Cryptocurrencies and Memes Over Traditional Investments " width="1280" height="400" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/cryptoww3221.jpg 1280w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/cryptoww3221-300x94.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/cryptoww3221-1024x320.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/cryptoww3221-768x240.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/cryptoww3221-696x218.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/cryptoww3221-1068x334.jpg 1068w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" />
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <span style="font-weight: 400;">With things like meme assets, cryptocurrencies, and NFTs at the forefront of investment, Gambler’s Pick says that zoomers deal with high-risk investments better than older generations. </span>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <span style="font-weight: 400;">“Baby boomers (and older respondents) tended to prefer to be a little safer with their investments,” the Gambler’s Pick researchers detail. Rather than technical analysis and stock fundamentals, Gambler’s Pick said Gen Z would rather take “tips and opinions” from Reddit, social media, and family and friends.</span>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <span style="font-weight: 400;">Lastly, the study with 872 respondents shows that zoomers believe that markets are manipulated and high-net-worth individuals and institutions rule the roost. </span>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <span style="font-weight: 400;">“Generally, baby boomers (and older) were a little more skeptical of these theories, but the younger generations were pretty sure there’s some truth behind them,” the study’s researchers concluded. </span>
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <em><strong>What do you think about Generation Z liking cryptocurrencies, memes, and NFTs over traditional investments like stocks? Let us know what you think about this subject in the comments section below. </strong></em>
  </p>
</div>
